    <string name="rules_goal_title">Goal</string>
    <string name="rules_goal_text">Sink all ten enemy ships before the computer sinks yours.</string>
    <string name="rules_fleet_title">Fleet</string>
    <string name="rules_fleet_text">Each side has 10 ships on a 10×10 board: one 4-deck, two 3-deck, three 2-deck and four 1-deck ships. Ships are straight lines and may not touch each other, not even at the corners.</string>
    <string name="rules_setup_title">Placing ships</string>
    <string name="rules_setup_text">Pick a ship, choose the direction and tap the cell where the ship should start. Tap a placed ship to remove it. \"Random\" places the whole fleet for you. When all ships are in place, press \"Start battle\".</string>
    <string name="rules_turns_title">Battle</string>
    <string name="rules_turns_text">Tap a cell in enemy waters to fire. If you hit, you shoot again; after a miss the computer takes its turn. When a ship is sunk, the cells around it are marked automatically because there can be no ships there. The last shot is outlined in yellow.</string>
    <string name="rules_marks_title">Board symbols</string>
    <string name="rules_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="rules_tips_text">Look for big ships first by shooting in a checkerboard pattern. After a hit, try the neighbouring cells to find out which way the ship goes.</string>
